      "confidence_note": "Remain stopped for the applicable front-facing red signals and occupied crosswalk. The supplied ego record reports zero speed, so maintaining the current center satisfies the proposed stop without instantaneous braking. The target is an allowed center corridor along the current approach, including the initial center; it is not a stopping box. Its rearward extent follows the approach visible in the rear cameras and is not an instruction to reverse. Road and object distances are conditional estimates from camera angular geometry and height assuming approximately level pavement, visible foot/road contacts, lane and curb layout, and learned pedestrian and vehicle dimensions. They are not calibrated ground-plane measurements. Negligible recorded ego motion supplies no useful triangulation. Road uncertainty represents curb/lane-placement error; object uncertainties represent residual coordinate and size error, separately from future motion. The crosswalk group aggregates the visible front pedestrians, their cart, and pedestrians at the left entrance; no point position or common velocity is asserted. The repeated polygon is deliberately an adopted whole-horizon swept envelope, not a stationary-body prediction: it contains bodies and cart during continued crossing, pauses, and reversal along the crosswalk, assuming walking speeds up to about 2 m/s and no departure toward the ego outside the longitudinal crosswalk band. Its lateral extent accommodates the currently visible left-side entrants and five seconds of crossing; its longitudinal extent includes foot-contact depth spread and modest longitudinal walking deviation. Repetition sacrifices temporal precision but retains that same conditional sweep for every interval. Historical front images support left-to-right walking, whereas the side views are asynchronous single observations; stationary ego compensation does not establish vehicle velocities. Rear pickup and truck stopping, creeping, and acceleration, the adjacent sedan's release or lateral intrusion, and continuing or turning intersection traffic remain unresolved over five seconds. Their occupancy is null rather than an invented stationary envelope. Nearby occluded entrants and those unresolved vehicle futures prevent a credible complete finite intrusion model, so unbounded_unknown remains true. The finite road hypothesis repairs the absent local-road estimate, but does not resolve the previous planning failure or establish collision-free verification."
